{"id":"mahabharata-9-028","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":28,"title":"अष्टाविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 28 · The last remnant and Sanjaya's capture","summary":{"en":"The Kauravas press forward again and Sahadeva and Arjuna kill many, and as the sun sets Duryodhana's few warriors flee. Sanjaya is taken prisoner, and Vidura bids Yuyutsu to take the women of the royal household into the city.","kn":"ಕೌರವರು ಮತ್ತೆ ಮುನ್ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಸಹದೇವ, ಅರ್ಜುನರು ಅನೇಕರನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಸೂರ್ಯಾಸ್ತದ ವೇಳೆ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಕೆಲವೇ ವೀರರು ಓಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸಂಜಯ ಬಂಧಿಯಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಾಜಮನೆತನದ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರನ್ನು ನಗರಕ್ಕೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯಲು ವಿದುರ ಯುಯುತ್ಸುವಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कौरव फिर आगे बढ़ते हैं, सहदेव और अर्जुन बहुतों को मारते हैं, और सूर्यास्त पर दुर्योधन के गिने-चुने योद्धा भाग जाते हैं। संजय बन्दी बनाए जाते हैं, और विदुर युयुत्सु से राजपरिवार की स्त्रियों को नगर ले जाने को कहते हैं।","te":"కౌరవులు మళ్లీ ముందుకు సాగుతారు; సహదేవుడు, అర్జునుడు అనేకులను చంపుతారు, సూర్యాస్తమయ వేళ దుర్యోధనుని కొద్ది వీరులు పారిపోతారు. సంజయుడు బందీ అవుతాడు; రాజకుటుంబ స్త్రీలను నగరానికి తీసుకెళ్లమని విదురుడు యుయుత్సునికి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"கௌரவர் மீண்டும் முன்னேற, சகதேவனும் அர்ஜுனனும் பலரைக் கொல்ல, சூரிய அஸ்தமன நேரத்தில் துரியோதனனின் சில வீரர் ஓடுகின்றனர். சஞ்சயன் சிறைப்பிடிக்கப்பட, அரச குடும்பப் பெண்களை நகருக்கு அழைத்துச் செல்லும்படி விதுரர் யுயுத்சுவுக்குக் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"കൗരവർ വീണ്ടും മുന്നേറുന്നു; സഹദേവനും അർജുനനും പലരെയും കൊല്ലുന്നു. സൂര്യൻ അസ്തമിക്കുമ്പോൾ ദുര്യോധനന്റെ ശേഷിച്ച കുറച്ചു യോദ്ധാക്കൾ ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു. സഞ്ജയൻ ബന്ധിയാക്കപ്പെടുന്നു; രാജകുടുംബത്തിലെ സ്ത്രീകളെ നഗരത്തിലേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോകാൻ വിദുരർ യുയുത്സുവിനോട് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.28; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धा महाराज सौबलस्य पदानुगाः ।\nत्यक्त्वा जीवितमाक्रन्दे पाण्डवान्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shakuni's followers, enraged, O great king, gave up hope of life and surrounded the Pandavas in the uproar."}},{"n":2,"text":"तानर्जुनः प्रत्यगृह्णात्सहदेवजये धृतः ।\nभीमसेनश्च तेजस्वी क्रुद्धाशीविषदर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, set on Sahadeva's victory, met them, and so did the radiant Bhimasena, looking like an angry venomous snake."}},{"n":3,"text":"शक्त्यृष्टिप्रासहस्तानां सहदेवं जिघांसताम् ।\nसंकल्पमकरोन्मोघं गाण्डीवेन धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Against those who held spears, darts and lances and wished to kill Sahadeva, Dhananjaya made their intent fruitless with the Gandiva."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रगृहीतायुधान्बाहून्योधानामभिधावताम् ।\nभल्लैश्चिच्छेद बीभत्सुः शिरांस्यपि हयानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the warriors rushed on with weapons raised, Bibhatsu cut off their arms with broad-headed arrows, and their heads and horses too."}},{"n":5,"text":"ते हताः प्रत्यपद्यन्त वसुधां विगतासवः ।\nत्वरिता लोकवीरेण प्रहताः सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down, they lay lifeless on the earth, hurried to death by Savyasachin, the hero of the world."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा दृष्ट्वा स्वबलसंक्षयम् ।\nहतशेषान्समानीय क्रुद्धो रथशतान्विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, seeing his force destroyed, enraged, gathered the remnant, O lord, hundreds of chariots,"}},{"n":7,"text":"कुञ्जरांश्च हयांश्चैव पादातांश्च परंतप ।\nउवाच सहितान्सर्वान्धार्तराष्ट्र इदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"elephants, horses and foot soldiers, O scorcher of foes, and the Dhartarashtra spoke these words to them all together:"}},{"n":8,"text":"समासाद्य रणे सर्वान्पाण्डवान्ससुहृद्गणान् ।\nपाञ्चाल्यं चापि सबलं हत्वा शीघ्रं निवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Meet all the Pandavas and their friends in the battle, kill the Panchala too with his force, and then quickly return.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्य ते शिरसा गृह्य वचनं युद्धदुर्मदाः ।\nप्रत्युद्ययू रणे पार्थांस्तव पुत्रस्य शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking his words on their heads, those men, wild for battle, advanced against the Parthas at your son's command."}},{"n":10,"text":"तानभ्यापततः शीघ्रं हतशेषान्महारणे ।\nशरैराशीविषाकारैः पाण्डवाः समवाकिरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the remnant rushed swiftly in that great battle, the Pandavas covered them with arrows shaped like venomous snakes."}},{"n":11,"text":"तत्सैन्यं भरतश्रेष्ठ मुहूर्तेन महात्मभिः ।\nअवध्यत रणं प्राप्य त्रातारं नाभ्यविन्दत ।\nप्रतिष्ठमानं तु भयान्नावतिष्ठत दंशितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army, O best of the Bharatas, was cut down in a moment by the great-souled men; having entered the battle, it found no protector. The armored men, setting out in fear, did not stand firm."}},{"n":12,"text":"अश्वैर्विपरिधावद्भिः सैन्येन रजसा वृते ।\nन प्राज्ञायन्त समरे दिशश्च प्रदिशस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With horses running in every direction and the army wrapped in dust, neither the quarters nor the intermediate directions could be told apart in the battle."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततस्तु पाण्डवानीकान्निःसृत्य बहवो जनाः ।\nअभ्यघ्नंस्तावकान्युद्धे मुहूर्तादिव भारत ।\nततो निःशेषमभवत्तत्सैन्यं तव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then many men came out of the Pandava force and struck your men in the battle, as if in a moment, O Bharata; and so your army was left without a remnant, O Bharata."}},{"n":14,"text":"अक्षौहिण्यः समेतास्तु तव पुत्रस्य भारत ।\nएकादश हता युद्धे ताः प्रभो पाण्डुसृञ्जयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eleven akshauhinis gathered for your son, O Bharata, were killed in battle by the Pandavas and Srinjayas, O lord."}},{"n":15,"text":"तेषु राजसहस्रेषु तावकेषु महात्मसु ।\nएको दुर्योधनो राजन्नदृश्यत भृशं क्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among those thousands of your great-souled kings, Duryodhana alone, O king, was seen, badly wounded."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो वीक्ष्य दिशः सर्वा दृष्ट्वा शून्यां च मेदिनीम् ।\nविहीनः सर्वयोधैश्च पाण्डवान्वीक्ष्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, looking in all directions and seeing the earth empty, deprived of all his warriors, looking at the Pandavas in the battle,"}},{"n":17,"text":"मुदितान्सर्वसिद्धार्थान्नर्दमानान्समन्ततः ।\nबाणशब्दरवांश्चैव श्रुत्वा तेषां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"joyful, with every aim achieved, roaring on every side, and hearing the sound of arrows from those great-souled men,"}},{"n":18,"text":"दुर्योधनो महाराज कश्मलेनाभिसंवृतः ।\nअपयाने मनश्चक्रे विहीनबलवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, O great king, overcome by dejection and robbed of force and mount, made up his mind to flee."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"निहते मामके सैन्ये निःशेषे शिबिरे कृते ।\nपाण्डवानां बलं सूत किं नु शेषमभूत्तदा ।\nएतन्मे पृच्छतो ब्रूहि कुशलो ह्यसि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When my army had been killed and the camp left empty, Sanjaya, what was then left of the Pandavas' force? Tell me when I ask this, for you are skilled."}},{"n":20,"text":"यच्च दुर्योधनो मन्दः कृतवांस्तनयो मम ।\nबलक्षयं तथा दृष्ट्वा स एकः पृथिवीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And what did Duryodhana, my foolish son, do, that lord of the earth, alone, seeing his army destroyed?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"रथानां द्वे सहस्रे तु सप्त नागशतानि च ।\nपञ्च चाश्वसहस्राणि पत्तीनां च शतं शताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two thousand chariots, seven hundred elephants, five thousand horses and a hundred hundreds of foot soldiers:"}},{"n":22,"text":"एतच्छेषमभूद्राजन्पाण्डवानां महद्बलम् ।\nपरिगृह्य हि यद्युद्धे धृष्टद्युम्नो व्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"this was all that remained of the Pandavas' great force, which Dhrishtadyumna took and stood with in the battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"एकाकी भरतश्रेष्ठ ततो दुर्योधनो नृपः ।\nनापश्यत्समरे कंचित्सहायं रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, O best of the Bharatas, that best of chariot-fighters, saw no companion at all in the battle, alone as he was."}},{"n":24,"text":"नर्दमानान्परांश्चैव स्वबलस्य च संक्षयम् ।\nहतं स्वहयमुत्सृज्य प्राङ्मुखः प्राद्रवद्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the enemies roaring and his own force destroyed, he abandoned his dead horse and fled in fear, facing east."}},{"n":25,"text":"एकादशचमूभर्ता पुत्रो दुर्योधनस्तव ।\nगदामादाय तेजस्वी पदातिः प्रस्थितो ह्रदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Duryodhana, who had commanded eleven armies, took up his mace and, radiant, set out on foot for a lake."}},{"n":26,"text":"नातिदूरं ततो गत्वा पद्भ्यामेव नराधिपः ।\nसस्मार वचनं क्षत्तुर्धर्मशीलस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gone not far on foot, the king remembered the words of Kshattri, wise and devoted to dharma."}},{"n":27,"text":"इदं नूनं महाप्राज्ञो विदुरो दृष्टवान्पुरा ।\nमहद्वैशसमस्माकं क्षत्रियाणां च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely the greatly wise Vidura foresaw this long ago: a great slaughter in battle for us and for the kshatriyas.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"एवं विचिन्तयानस्तु प्रविविक्षुर्ह्रदं नृपः ।\nदुःखसंतप्तहृदयो दृष्ट्वा राजन्बलक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking so, the king, wishing to enter the lake, his heart burning with grief at the destruction of his force, O king,"}},{"n":29,"text":"पाण्डवाश्च महाराज धृष्टद्युम्नपुरोगमाः ।\nअभ्यधावन्त संक्रुद्धास्तव राजन्बलं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"while the Pandavas, O great king, with Dhrishtadyumna at their head, enraged, ran at your force, O king."}},{"n":30,"text":"शक्त्यृष्टिप्रासहस्तानां बलानामभिगर्जताम् ।\nसंकल्पमकरोन्मोघं गाण्डीवेन धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Against those who roared, holding spears, darts and lances, Dhananjaya made their intent fruitless with the Gandiva."}},{"n":31,"text":"तान्हत्वा निशितैर्बाणैः सामात्यान्सह बन्धुभिः ।\nरथे श्वेतहये तिष्ठन्नर्जुनो बह्वशोभत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed them with sharp arrows, with their counselors and kinsmen, Arjuna, standing in his chariot with white horses, shone greatly."}},{"n":32,"text":"सुबलस्य हते पुत्रे सवाजिरथकुञ्जरे ।\nमहावनमिव छिन्नमभवत्तावकं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Subala's son was killed together with his horses, chariot and elephants, your force became like a great forest cut down."}},{"n":33,"text":"अनेकशतसाहस्रे बले दुर्योधनस्य ह ।\nनान्यो महारथो राजञ्जीवमानो व्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the force of Duryodhana, of many hundreds of thousands, no other great chariot-fighter, O king, was seen alive"}},{"n":34,"text":"द्रोणपुत्रादृते वीरात्तथैव कृतवर्मणः ।\nकृपाच्च गौतमाद्राजन्पार्थिवाच्च तवात्मजात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"except Drona's heroic son, Kritavarman, Kripa the Gautama, and your own son the king."}},{"n":35,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्तु मां दृष्ट्वा हसन्सात्यकिमब्रवीत् ।\nकिमनेन गृहीतेन नानेनार्थोऽस्ति जीवता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, seeing me, said laughing to Satyaki: \"What use is it to have taken this one? There is no purpose in his being alive.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नवचः श्रुत्वा शिनेर्नप्ता महारथः ।\nउद्यम्य निशितं खड्गं हन्तुं मामुद्यतस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Dhrishtadyumna's words, the great chariot-fighter, grandson of Shini, raised a sharp sword to kill me."}},{"n":37,"text":"तमागम्य महाप्राज्ञः कृष्णद्वैपायनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nमुच्यतां संजयो जीवन्न हन्तव्यः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the greatly wise Krishna Dvaipayana came up to him and said: \"Let Sanjaya go; he is not to be killed in any way.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"द्वैपायनवचः श्रुत्वा शिनेर्नप्ता कृताञ्जलिः ।\nततो मामब्रवीन्मुक्त्वा स्वस्ति संजय साधय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Dvaipayana's words, the grandson of Shini, hands folded, released me and said, \"Go in peace, Sanjaya, and see to your affairs.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"अनुज्ञातस्त्वहं तेन न्यस्तवर्मा निरायुधः ।\nप्रातिष्ठं येन नगरं सायाह्ने रुधिरोक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Permitted by him, I set out for the city in the evening, my armor laid down, without weapons and smeared with blood."}},{"n":40,"text":"क्रोशमात्रमपक्रान्तं गदापाणिमवस्थितम् ।\nएकं दुर्योधनं राजन्नपश्यं भृशविक्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"About a krosha away, O king, I saw Duryodhana alone, badly wounded, standing with mace in hand."}},{"n":41,"text":"स तु मामश्रुपूर्णाक्षो नाशक्नोदभिवीक्षितुम् ।\nउपप्रैक्षत मां दृष्ट्वा तदा दीनमवस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With eyes full of tears, he could not look at me; he only glanced at me, seeing me standing there in distress."}},{"n":42,"text":"तं चाहमपि शोचन्तं दृष्ट्वैकाकिनमाहवे ।\nमुहूर्तं नाशकं वक्तुं किंचिद्दुःखपरिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I, seeing him grieving alone after the battle, was overwhelmed with sorrow and could say nothing for a moment."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततोऽस्मै तदहं सर्वमुक्तवान्ग्रहणं तदा ।\nद्वैपायनप्रसादाच्च जीवतो मोक्षमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I told him everything: my capture, and my release from the battle alive by Dvaipayana's grace."}},{"n":44,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव च ध्यात्वा प्रतिलभ्य च चेतनाम् ।\nभ्रातॄंश्च सर्वसैन्यानि पर्यपृच्छत मां ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After thinking for a moment and regaining his senses, he asked me about his brothers and all the armies."}},{"n":45,"text":"तस्मै तदहमाचक्षं सर्वं प्रत्यक्षदर्शिवान् ।\nभ्रातॄंश्च निहतान्सर्वान्सैन्यं च विनिपातितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told him everything, as an eyewitness: that all his brothers were killed and his army struck down."}},{"n":46,"text":"त्रयः किल रथाः शिष्टास्तावकानां नराधिप ।\nइति प्रस्थानकाले मां कृष्णद्वैपायनोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Only three of your chariot-fighters remain, O lord of men,\" Krishna Dvaipayana told me as I was leaving."}},{"n":47,"text":"स दीर्घमिव निःश्वस्य विप्रेक्ष्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nअंसे मां पाणिना स्पृष्ट्वा पुत्रस्ते पर्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son, sighing deeply as it were and looking at me again and again, touched my shoulder with his hand and said:"}},{"n":48,"text":"त्वदन्यो नेह संग्रामे कश्चिज्जीवति संजय ।\nद्वितीयं नेह पश्यामि ससहायाश्च पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"No one but you is alive here in this battle, Sanjaya; I see no second one here, while the Pandavas have their allies."}},{"n":49,"text":"ब्रूयाः संजय राजानं प्रज्ञाचक्षुषमीश्वरम् ।\nदुर्योधनस्तव सुतः प्रविष्टो ह्रदमित्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell the king with the eye of wisdom, the lord, Sanjaya: 'Your son Duryodhana has entered a lake.'"}},{"n":50,"text":"सुहृद्भिस्तादृशैर्हीनः पुत्रैर्भ्रातृभिरेव च ।\nपाण्डवैश्च हृते राज्ये को नु जीवति मादृशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bereft of such friends, of sons and of brothers, and with the kingdom taken by the Pandavas, who like me would go on living?"}},{"n":51,"text":"आचक्षेथाः सर्वमिदं मां च मुक्तं महाहवात् ।\nअस्मिंस्तोयह्रदे सुप्तं जीवन्तं भृशविक्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell all this, and that I escaped the great battle and lie in this pool of water, alive, badly wounded.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा महाराज प्राविशत्तं ह्रदं नृपः ।\nअस्तम्भयत तोयं च मायया मनुजाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, O great king, the king entered that lake, and the lord of men stilled its water by his power of illusion."}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्मिन्ह्रदं प्रविष्टे तु त्रीन्रथाञ्श्रान्तवाहनान् ।\nअपश्यं सहितानेकस्तं देशं समुपेयुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had entered the lake, I saw three chariot-fighters with weary mounts, together, approaching that place."}},{"n":54,"text":"कृपं शारद्वतं वीरं द्रौणिं च रथिनां वरम् ।\nभोजं च कृतवर्माणं सहिताञ्शरविक्षतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were the hero Kripa, son of Sharadvat, Drona's son, best of chariot-fighters, and Kritavarman of the Bhojas, together and wounded by arrows."}},{"n":55,"text":"ते सर्वे मामभिप्रेक्ष्य तूर्णमश्वानचोदयन् ।\nउपयाय च मामूचुर्दिष्ट्या जीवसि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them, seeing me, quickly urged their horses on, came up to me and said, \"By good fortune you live, Sanjaya.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"अपृच्छंश्चैव मां सर्वे पुत्रं तव जनाधिपम् ।\nकच्चिद्दुर्योधनो राजा स नो जीवति संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And all of them asked me about your son the king: \"Is Duryodhana, our king, alive, Sanjaya?\""}},{"n":57,"text":"आख्यातवानहं तेभ्यस्तदा कुशलिनं नृपम् ।\nतच्चैव सर्वमाचक्षं यन्मां दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nह्रदं चैवाहमाचष्ट यं प्रविष्टो नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told them then that the king was well, and I told them all that Duryodhana had said to me, and the lake he had entered."}},{"n":58,"text":"अश्वत्थामा तु तद्राजन्निशम्य वचनं मम ।\nतं ह्रदं विपुलं प्रेक्ष्य करुणं पर्यदेवयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing my words, O king, Ashvatthama looked at that wide lake and lamented piteously:"}},{"n":59,"text":"अहो धिङ्न स जानाति जीवतोऽस्मान्नराधिपः ।\nपर्याप्ता हि वयं तेन सह योधयितुं परान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ah, shame! The king does not know we are alive. Together with him we are enough to fight the enemy.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"ते तु तत्र चिरं कालं विलप्य च महारथाः ।\nप्राद्रवन्रथिनां श्रेष्ठा दृष्ट्वा पाण्डुसुतान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those great chariot-fighters, best of chariot-fighters, having lamented there for a long time, fled on seeing the sons of Pandu in the battle."}},{"n":61,"text":"ते तु मां रथमारोप्य कृपस्य सुपरिष्कृतम् ।\nसेनानिवेशमाजग्मुर्हतशेषास्त्रयो रथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The three surviving chariot-fighters put me in Kripa's well-furnished chariot and came to the army camp."}},{"n":62,"text":"तत्र गुल्माः परित्रस्ताः सूर्ये चास्तमिते सति ।\nसर्वे विचुक्रुशुः श्रुत्वा पुत्राणां तव संक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, as the sun set, the troops in the camp, terrified, all cried out on hearing of the destruction of your sons."}},{"n":63,"text":"ततो वृद्धा महाराज योषितां रक्षणो नराः ।\nराजदारानुपादाय प्रययुर्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then old men, guardians of the women, took the king's wives, O great king, and set out for the city."}},{"n":64,"text":"तत्र विक्रोशतीनां च रुदतीनां च सर्वशः ।\nप्रादुरासीन्महाञ्शब्दः श्रुत्वा तद्बलसंक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great sound arose there from the women, crying out and weeping on every side, on hearing the destruction of that force."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततस्ता योषितो राजन्क्रन्दन्त्यो वै मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nकुरर्य इव शब्देन नादयन्त्यो महीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those women, wailing again and again, O king, made the ground resound with cries like ospreys."}},{"n":66,"text":"आजघ्नुः करजैश्चापि पाणिभिश्च शिरांस्युत ।\nलुलुवुश्च तदा केशान्क्रोशन्त्यस्तत्र तत्र ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"They struck their heads with their nails and hands, and tore out their hair, crying out here and there."}},{"n":67,"text":"हाहाकारविनादिन्यो विनिघ्नन्त्य उरांसि च ।\nक्रोशन्त्यस्तत्र रुरुदुः क्रन्दमाना विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wailing \"Alas, alas!\" and beating their breasts, they cried and wept, O lord of the people."}},{"n":68,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनामात्याः साश्रुकण्ठा भृशातुराः ।\nराजदारानुपादाय प्रययुर्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana's counselors, their throats choked with tears and in deep distress, took the king's wives and set out for the city."}},{"n":69,"text":"वेत्रजर्झरहस्ताश्च द्वाराध्यक्षा विशां पते ।\nशयनीयानि शुभ्राणि स्पर्ध्यास्तरणवन्ति च ।\nसमादाय ययुस्तूर्णं नगरं दाररक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Doorkeepers with canes and staffs in hand, O lord of the people, took bright couches and rich spreads and quickly went to the city, guarding the women."}},{"n":70,"text":"आस्थायाश्वतरीयुक्तान्स्यन्दनानपरे जनाः ।\nस्वान्स्वान्दारानुपादाय प्रययुर्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others mounted chariots yoked with mules, took their own wives and went toward the city."}},{"n":71,"text":"अदृष्टपूर्वा या नार्यो भास्करेणापि वेश्मसु ।\nददृशुस्ता महाराज जना यान्तीः पुरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women who had never been seen even by the sun in their houses were seen by people as they went to the city."}},{"n":72,"text":"ताः स्त्रियो भरतश्रेष्ठ सौकुमार्यसमन्विताः ।\nप्रययुर्नगरं तूर्णं हतस्वजनबान्धवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those delicate women, O best of the Bharatas, their kinsmen and relatives slain, went quickly to the city."}},{"n":73,"text":"आ गोपालाविपालेभ्यो द्रवन्तो नगरं प्रति ।\nययुर्मनुष्याः संभ्रान्ता भीमसेनभयार्दिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men, from cowherds and shepherds on up, ran toward the city in confusion, tormented by fear of Bhimasena."}},{"n":74,"text":"अपि चैषां भयं तीव्रं पार्थेभ्योऽभूत्सुदारुणम् ।\nप्रेक्षमाणास्तदान्योन्यमाधावन्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They also had a dreadful, intense fear of the Parthas, and looking at one another they ran toward the city."}},{"n":75,"text":"तस्मिंस्तदा वर्तमाने विद्रवे भृशदारुणे ।\nयुयुत्सुः शोकसंमूढः प्राप्तकालमचिन्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that terrible flight went on, Yuyutsu, bewildered by sorrow, thought about what the time required:"}},{"n":76,"text":"जितो दुर्योधनः संख्ये पाण्डवैर्भीमविक्रमैः ।\nएकादशचमूभर्ता भ्रातरश्चास्य सूदिताः ।\nहताश्च कुरवः सर्वे भीष्मद्रोणपुरःसराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana has been beaten in battle by the Pandavas of fearsome valor, he who commanded eleven armies; his brothers have been slain, and all the Kurus, with Bhishma and Drona at their head, are dead."}},{"n":77,"text":"अहमेको विमुक्तस्तु भाग्ययोगाद्यदृच्छया ।\nविद्रुतानि च सर्वाणि शिबिराणि समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I alone have been spared, by good fortune and chance. All the camps have fled on every side."}},{"n":78,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य सचिवा ये केचिदवशेषिताः ।\nराजदारानुपादाय व्यधावन्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever counselors of Duryodhana remain have taken the king's wives and run toward the city."}},{"n":79,"text":"प्राप्तकालमहं मन्ये प्रवेशं तैः सहाभिभो ।\nयुधिष्ठिरमनुज्ञाप्य भीमसेनं तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the time has come, O lord, for me to enter with them, once Yudhishthira and Bhimasena have given leave.\""}},{"n":80,"text":"एतमर्थं महाबाहुरुभयोः स न्यवेदयत् ।\nतस्य प्रीतोऽभवद्राजा नित्यं करुणवेदिता ।\nपरिष्वज्य महाबाहुर्वैश्यापुत्रं व्यसर्जयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strong-armed man reported this matter to them both. The king, ever compassionate, was pleased with him, and the strong-armed Yudhishthira embraced the Vaishya woman's son and let him go."}},{"n":81,"text":"ततः स रथमास्थाय द्रुतमश्वानचोदयत् ।\nअसंभावितवांश्चापि राजदारान्पुरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he mounted his chariot and quickly urged on the horses, and escorted the royal women toward the city."}},{"n":82,"text":"तैश्चैव सहितः क्षिप्रमस्तं गच्छति भास्करे ।\nप्रविष्टो हास्तिनपुरं बाष्पकण्ठोऽश्रुलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With them, as the sun was setting, he quickly entered Hastinapura, his throat choked and his eyes full of tears."}},{"n":83,"text":"अपश्यत महाप्राज्ञं विदुरं साश्रुलोचनम् ।\nराज्ञः समीपान्निष्क्रान्तं शोकोपहतचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the greatly wise Vidura, tears in his eyes and his mind struck by grief, coming out from the king's side."}},{"n":84,"text":"तमब्रवीत्सत्यधृतिः प्रणतं त्वग्रतः स्थितम् ।\nअस्मिन्कुरुक्षये वृत्ते दिष्ट्या त्वं पुत्र जीवसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vidura, firm in truth, said to him as he stood bowing in front: \"In this destruction of the Kurus, by good fortune you live, my son."}},{"n":85,"text":"विना राज्ञः प्रवेशाद्वै किमसि त्वमिहागतः ।\nएतन्मे कारणं सर्वं विस्तरेण निवेदय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why have you come here, without the king having entered? Tell me all the reason in detail.\""}},{"text":"युयुत्सुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yuyutsu said:"}},{"n":86,"text":"निहते शकुनौ तात सज्ञातिसुतबान्धवे ।\nहतशेषपरीवारो राजा दुर्योधनस्ततः ।\nस्वकं स हयमुत्सृज्य प्राङ्मुखः प्राद्रवद्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When Shakuni was killed, father, with his kinsmen, sons and relatives, King Duryodhana, with his retinue reduced to a remnant, abandoned his own horse and fled in fear, facing east."}},{"n":87,"text":"अपक्रान्ते तु नृपतौ स्कन्धावारनिवेशनात् ।\nभयव्याकुलितं सर्वं प्राद्रवन्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king had gone from the camp, everyone, thrown into confusion by fear, fled toward the city."}},{"n":88,"text":"ततो राज्ञः कलत्राणि भ्रातॄणां चास्य सर्वशः ।\nवाहनेषु समारोप्य स्त्र्यध्यक्षाः प्राद्रवन्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the women's overseers put the wives of the king and of his brothers on carriages and fled in fear."}},{"n":89,"text":"ततोऽहं समनुज्ञाप्य राजानं सहकेशवम् ।\nप्रविष्टो हास्तिनपुरं रक्षँल्लोकाद्धि वाच्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I took leave of the king and of Keshava and entered Hastinapura, guarding against the world's reproach.\""}},{"n":90,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु वचनं वैश्यापुत्रेण भाषितम् ।\nप्राप्तकालमिति ज्ञात्वा विदुरः सर्वधर्मवित् ।\nअपूजयदमेयात्मा युयुत्सुं वाक्यकोविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words spoken by the Vaishya woman's son, and knowing the time had come, Vidura, knower of all dharma and of immeasurable spirit, praised Yuyutsu, skilled in speech."}},{"n":91,"text":"प्राप्तकालमिदं सर्वं भवतो भरतक्षये ।\nअद्य त्वमिह विश्रान्तः श्वोऽभिगन्ता युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All this has come at the right time for you in this destruction of the Bharatas. Rest here today, and tomorrow you will go to Yudhishthira.\""}},{"n":92,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा वचनं विदुरः सर्वधर्मवित् ।\nयुयुत्सुं समनुज्ञाप्य प्रविवेश नृपक्षयम् ।\nयुयुत्सुरपि तां रात्रिं स्वगृहे न्यवसत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said just this, Vidura, knower of all dharma, gave Yuyutsu leave and went into the king's house of grief; and Yuyutsu spent that night in his own house."}}]}]}